From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 04:02:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/28] node-executor: propagate exhausted OCC callback errors

The mutation runner already applies its bounded OCC retry policy before
returning OptimisticConcurrencyControlFailure as HTTP 503. Treating that
response as a generic transient failure in the Node callback loop restarts
the whole mutation budget up to five times.

Inspect intermediate 503 bodies for the structured OCC code and propagate
a positively identified error through the existing caller error handler.
Keep ordinary 5xx and transport retries, including the stable mutation
identifier used to deduplicate committed results.

Bound body inspection by size and time, consume the original stream rather
than cloning it, and honor action disposal without waiting for cancellation
to finish. Unclassifiable responses retain the transient retry policy.

Cover OCC propagation, retry budgets and identifiers, malformed and stalled
bodies, UTF-8 boundaries, and action disposal with focused regression tests.
